---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {getProject} from '../data/tech-projects';
import ConstructionStudy from './TechConstructionStudy.astro';
import ReviewStudy from './TechReviewStudy.astro';
interface Props {slug:string}
const project=getProject(Astro.props.slug);
const base = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/`;
---
<Layout title={`${project.name} — Engineering Case Study / ICY TECH`} description={project.summary}>
<section class="tech-shell tech-hero"><a href={`${base}projects/`}>← Technical ecosystem</a><p class="tech-eyebrow">{String(project.rank).padStart(2,'0')} / {project.category}</p><h1>{project.name}</h1><p class="tech-lead">{project.summary}</p><ul class="tech-tags">{project.stack.map(item=><li>{item}</li>)}</ul><p class="tech-status">Audit snapshot: {project.version}</p><p class="tech-note">Independent implementation and integration, supported by coding agents and established upstream libraries. No claim of upstream model/framework authorship or paid employment is implied.</p></section>
<section class="tech-shell tech-section"><h2>The engineering problem</h2><p class="tech-lead">{project.problem}</p><h3>Why this work is featured</h3><p>{project.why}</p><figure class="tech-diagram"><ol>{project.flow.map((step,index)=><li><span class="tech-eyebrow">{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><strong>{step}</strong></li>)}</ol><figcaption>Conceptual architecture, curated from source review. An explanatory diagram, not a runtime trace.</figcaption></figure><h3>Decisions that matter</h3><ul>{project.decisions.map(decision=><li>{decision}</li>)}</ul></section>
<section class="tech-shell tech-section"><p class="tech-eyebrow">Verification ledger</p><h2>What the evidence actually supports.</h2><ul>{project.evidence.map(item=><li>{item}</li>)}</ul><details class="tech-note"><summary>Implementation reference map</summary><p>Relative source modules reviewed. Source stays private unless explicitly linked; local filesystem paths and operational receipts are excluded.</p><ul>{project.source.map(file=><li><code>{file}</code></li>)}</ul></details><h3>Boundaries & remaining work</h3><ul>{project.limitations.map(item=><li>{item}</li>)}</ul></section>
<section class="tech-shell tech-section"><p class="tech-eyebrow">Demonstration status</p><h2>See the work, honestly.</h2><p class="tech-lead">{project.demonstration}</p>{project.live && <p><a class="tech-button" href={project.live} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit public application ↗</a></p>}{project.repository && <p><a href={project.repository}>Inspect public source ↗</a></p>}{project.image && <figure><img src={`${base}${project.image}`} width="1000" height="650" style="width:auto;max-width:100%;height:auto;max-height:900px;object-fit:contain" alt={project.imageCaption} loading="lazy"/><figcaption>{project.imageCaption}</figcaption></figure>}{project.slug==='visual-lab' && <ConstructionStudy />}{project.slug==='music-archive' && <ReviewStudy />}<p class="tech-muted">No local service, private repository, account token, personal dataset or operational registry is connected.</p></section>
<section class="tech-shell tech-section"><h2>Related engineering</h2><div class="tech-grid">{project.related.map(slug=>{const other=getProject(slug);return <article class="tech-card"><h3><a href={`${base}projects/${slug}/`}>{other.name}</a></h3><p>{other.summary}</p></article>})}</div><p class="tech-muted">Related links express shared concerns; they do not assert a deployed integration unless explicitly documented.</p></section>
</Layout>